# Share queries format (Ashutosh)

Whenever the user asks to share queries (SQL verify / checklist / seed / UPDATE / grep packs they will paste), use **this shape only**.

## Do

- One fenced `sql` (or `bash` for greps) block. Everything in that one block.
- Numbered `-- N short purpose` comment on the line **immediately above** each SQL statement. For bash greps use `# N short purpose`.
- **Prod log greps:** node-prefixed paths in `prod-log-grep-format.mdc`. Do not use `/apps/applogs/dsa/` with no node IP.
- Each statement stays a **one-liner** (fully qualified `schema.table`).
- Ready to execute. Hardcode known env values. Call out any remaining `<placeholder>` before the block.

```sql
-- 1 Schema exists
SHOW DATABASES LIKE 'ddp_task_allocation';

-- 2 TASK-ALLOCATION registered (not localhost)
SELECT sm.name, sm.endpoint FROM platform_master.service_master sm WHERE sm.name='TASK-ALLOCATION';
```

## Do not

- Split the pack across chat as separate snippets, tables of SQL, or prose-wrapped queries
- Pretty-print a statement across multiple lines inside the block
- Put the number in markdown (`### 1`) instead of an SQL `--` comment
